     "abstract": "<p>♦ Most common in middle age.</p><p>♦ Classically ECRB affected laterally, Pronator teres and FCR medially.</p><p>♦ Histology is angiofibroblastic hyperplasia-tendinosis, not inflammation.</p><p>♦ Treatments include physical and injection therapy, as well as surgery.</p><p>♦ Concomitant ulna neuritis medially reduces success of surgery.</p>",
